WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.398 --> 00:00:02.067
What happens to open norms?

2
00:00:03.355 --> 00:00:08.098
We propose that nothing
happens differently than now.

3
00:00:08.098 --> 00:00:11.240
We deal with open norms in two ways.

4
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.263
The norm may stay open in the law,

5
00:00:15.263 --> 00:00:17.464
but implementation policy
still makes choices.

6
00:00:18.302 --> 00:00:20.864
Or in lower laws and regulations.

7
00:00:20.864 --> 00:00:24.587
Sometimes only in a work
instruction or in software

8
00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:28.609
is a choice made that
closes the open norm.

9
00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:32.932
RegelRecht doesn't change that.

10
00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.074
The only difference is that we make it

11
00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:41.476
Legislation and implementation
policy become machine-executable.

12
00:00:41.476 --> 00:00:45.857
All the choices that fill in open norms,

13
00:00:45.857 --> 00:00:50.879
we make explicit and transparent.

14
00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:56.140
That makes it traceable
how choices were made,

15
00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.441
and makes them reproducible.

16
00:00:58.441 --> 00:01:04.465
The other way of filling in open norms:

17
00:01:04.465 --> 00:01:07.727
there is room for, say, a

18
00:01:07.727 --> 00:01:11.169
decision-making official to make a choice.

19
00:01:11.169 --> 00:01:14.211
We don't change that either.

20
00:01:14.211 --> 00:01:18.394
An example of this is in

21
00:01:18.394 --> 00:01:21.636
asylum law,

22
00:01:23.695 --> 00:01:27.578
the concept of partner. Sometimes it
is very hard to prove that you are

23
00:01:27.578 --> 00:01:28.478
partners.

24
00:01:28.478 --> 00:01:32.921
For example if you may not
marry in your country of origin.

25
00:01:32.921 --> 00:01:37.244
Then evidence has to be provided.

26
00:01:37.244 --> 00:01:40.506
Holiday photos can count as
evidence that you are already

27
00:01:41.326 --> 00:01:47.410
Then it is up to an official to

28
00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:53.394
assess those photos and conclude that

29
00:01:53.394 --> 00:01:55.875
it is plausible that
two people are partners.

30
00:01:57.203 --> 00:01:59.544
With RegelRecht that
stays exactly the same.

31
00:01:59.544 --> 00:02:03.424
That then becomes a data point.

32
00:02:03.424 --> 00:02:07.885
The plausibility of a partner.

33
00:02:07.885 --> 00:02:12.746
That data point feeds into
the statutes and regulations.

34
00:02:12.746 --> 00:02:17.287
But getting to that data
point, the human assessment,

35
00:02:17.287 --> 00:02:19.628
we are not changing.

36
00:02:19.628 --> 00:02:20.428
That is still the case.
